  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), \\(\\angle B=40^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle C=60^\\circ\\). The bisector \\(AD\\) of \\(\\angle BAC\\) intersects \\(BC\\) at \\(D\\). Find the measure of \\(\\angle ADC\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "80",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle BAC=80^\\circ\\), and \\(\\angle BAD=40^\\circ\\). Since \\(\\angle ADC\\) is an exterior angle of \\(\\triangle ABD\\), \\(\\angle ADC=\\angle B+\\angle BAD=40^\\circ+40^\\circ=80^\\circ\\).",
